    {
      "id": "Emj8Us9XFDxeu0AXUMrlj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1579.2189357139175,
      "y": 21765.616064647616,
      "width": 573,
      "height": 945,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#846358",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ap",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 127788874,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 799304918,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783530062660,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) Example inputs and how Kafka reads them\n        Example 1\n        You type:\n                id1:apple\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = id1\n                value = apple\n\n\n        Example 2\n        You type:\n                emp101:salary updated\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = emp101\n                value = salary updated\n\n\n        Example 3\n        You type:\n                order55:payment done\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = order55\n                value = payment done\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) Example inputs and how Kafka reads them\n        Example 1\n        You type:\n                id1:apple\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = id1\n                value = apple\n\n\n        Example 2\n        You type:\n                emp101:salary updated\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = emp101\n                value = salary updated\n\n\n        Example 3\n        You type:\n                order55:payment done\n\n        Kafka stores:\n                key = order55\n                value = payment done\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Kjum2JWMdXrIpWvNfZdPk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 158.77470150167812,
      "y": 22366.504906064714,
      "width": 831,
      "height": 735,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#846358",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 479741718,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 397447882,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783530107472,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4) Why Kafka needs the key\n\n        Kafka messages are actually like this:\n\n        Key   -> optional\n        Value -> actual message data\n\n\n        Kafka uses the key mainly for partition selection.\n\n        Example topic has 3 partitions.\n        If you send:\n\n        user1:login\n        user1:logout\n        user1:buy product\n\n        all messages with key user1 usually go to the same partition.\n\n        That helps keep order for the same user/order/customer.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4) Why Kafka needs the key\n\n        Kafka messages are actually like this:\n\n        Key   -> optional\n        Value -> actual message data\n\n\n        Kafka uses the key mainly for partition selection.\n\n        Example topic has 3 partitions.\n        If you send:\n\n        user1:login\n        user1:logout\n        user1:buy product\n\n        all messages with key user1 usually go to the same partition.\n\n        That helps keep order for the same user/order/customer.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JuG1S7s0-AvOHWvm2hgwr",
      "type": "rectangle",
